{% comment %}
  The doctor card in Doctor Select (Step 2 of 5), matching the Figma spec
  exactly (node 544:3781) — rebuilt as a fully static mockup per explicit
  instruction, replacing the earlier real-backend-data version (name +
  generic "Ayurveda Physician" subtitle only, since /api/public/doctors
  only returns { id, name }). This card intentionally shows content
  (degree, languages, experience, specialty tags, next slot, price) the
  real API doesn't provide yet — it's a mockup, not live data.

  DEFAULT (unselected) appearance updated to match node 690:6562 —
  120px photo (was 76px), degree+experience grouped on one line with
  languages below (was all three stacked one-per-line), and a cream-
  tinted meta icon badge (was plain white). Explicit instruction: the
  existing --selected ("on click") treatment is untouched — see
  .kal-doctor-card--selected .kal-doctor-card__meta-icon in the CSS,
  which overrides the icon badge back to white so the selected look
  stays exactly as it was.

  Accepts:
  - name: {String} e.g. "Dr. Neethu Jayachandran"
  - degree: {String} e.g. "BAMS"
  - languages: {String} pre-joined, e.g. "English &middot; Hindi &middot; Malayalam"
  - experience: {String} full phrase, e.g. "12 yrs experience"
  - tags: {String} comma-separated specialty tags, e.g. "Anxiety,Stress Management"
  - next_slot: {String} e.g. "Today, 10:30 AM"
  - price: {String} e.g. "&#8377;500" — pre-formatted, not a bare number
  - selected: {Boolean} true for the tan-border/gradient/shadow highlighted
    treatment (same visual language as Concern Select's selected row)
  - photo_url: {String} doctor photo URL — DUMMY/placeholder, no real
    doctor photos exist yet

  Usage:
  {% render 'kal-booking-flow-doctor-card',
    name: 'Dr. Neethu Jayachandran',
    degree: 'BAMS',
    languages: 'English &middot; Hindi &middot; Malayalam',
    experience: '12 yrs experience',
    tags: 'Anxiety,Stress Management,Diabetes Care,Preventive Health',
    next_slot: 'Today, 10:30 AM',
    price: '&#8377;500',
    selected: true
  %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign tag_list = tags | default: '' | split: ','
-%}

<button
  type="button"
  class="kal-doctor-card {% if selected %}kal-doctor-card--selected{% endif %}"
  data-kal-doctor-name="{{ name }}"
>
  <span class="kal-doctor-card__top">
    <span class="kal-doctor-card__body">
      <span class="kal-doctor-card__photo">
        {%- if photo_url != blank -%}
          <img src="{{ photo_url }}" alt="{{ name }}" loading="lazy">
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
      <span class="kal-doctor-card__info">
        <span class="kal-doctor-card__name">{{ name }}</span>
        <span class="kal-doctor-card__meta-row">
          <span class="kal-doctor-card__meta-icon">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'doctor-education' -%}
          </span>
          {{ degree }}
        </span>
        <span class="kal-doctor-card__meta-row">
          <span class="kal-doctor-card__meta-icon">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'doctor-language' -%}
          </span>
          {{ languages }}
        </span>
        <span class="kal-doctor-card__meta-row">
          <span class="kal-doctor-card__meta-icon">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'doctor-experience' -%}
          </span>
          {{ experience }}
        </span>
      </span>
    </span>

    {%- if tag_list.size > 0 -%}
      <span class="kal-doctor-card__tags">
        {%- for tag in tag_list -%}
          <span class="kal-doctor-card__tag">{{ tag | strip }}</span>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </span>

  <span class="kal-doctor-card__footer">
    <span class="kal-doctor-card__next-slot">Next slot - <strong>{{ next_slot }}</strong></span>
    <span class="kal-doctor-card__price">{{ price }}</span>
  </span>
</button>
